592186082297} :answer-field/id #uuid "a88af808-6d41-5393-8859-9acb647cc2cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082295}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5078528-4e53-5684-a818-c4b067e4dfab" :question/math-academy-id "q-6684" :question/problem "Is the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$, for $x\\ne 0$, even, odd, or neither?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that\n\n- a function is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x,$ while\n\n- a function is odd if $f(-x)=-f(x)$ for all $x.$\n\nComputing $f(-x)$ for the given function and comparing it to $f(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\frac{1}{(-x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=f(x),$ the function is even.\n\nLastly, we compute $-f(x)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-f(x) & =-(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)\\ne -f(x),$ the function is not odd.\n\nTherefore, the function is only even."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2a0ef31-ab1d-5eb3-8116-471779b5b87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082332} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a92b0a-a567-5ac3-9afb-60c86335a3ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{61}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082333} {:answer/id #uuid "42d14ff7-4b0b-50e0-bb3c-a6a55a99c3b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{65}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082334} {:answer/id #uuid "78df4990-7698-5811-aa82-2d67e2d593e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{63}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082335} {:answer/id #uuid "79404